# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is gitignored; this file is committed.
#
#   cd docker && cp .env.example .env
#
# No IPs are hardcoded in committed files (project convention), which is why the
# defaults below are placeholders and not the values from anyone's bench.

# --- Images ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Image name convention: ${REGISTRY}/demo-aquila-<service>:${TAG}
# `local` builds and stays on this machine. For the hil mode you need a registry
# the module can reach, or `docker save | ssh ... docker load` (guia §9).
REGISTRY=local
TAG=dev

# --- ROS 2 / DDS -----------------------------------------------------------
# MUST be identical on host and module. A domain mismatch produces "the topics
# do not appear" with no error message anywhere — it is the single most common
# cause of a dead host<->module link.
#
# 69 comes from scripts/env.sh, the project's existing environment contract, so
# containers and host-native tooling land on the same domain by default. Note
# the ML3.5 guide's example says 42; the repo value wins to avoid a second
# domain existing in the project.
ROS_DOMAIN_ID=69

# Explicit DDS peers. Multicast is disabled in the CycloneDDS XMLs because it
# commonly dies on Wi-Fi and managed switches.
#
# For learn mode (everything on this host) these can stay as-is: the containers
# share the host network namespace and find each other without peers.
# For hil mode BOTH must be real, reachable addresses.
#
# Find them with `ip -br addr` on the host and on the module.
HOST_IP=192.168.1.10
MODULE_IP=192.168.1.20

# --- Graphics (host only) --------------------------------------------------
# Consumed by the sim and viz services. Never set on the module — nothing
# graphical runs there (CLAUDE.md rule 1).
#
# Before starting, allow the container to reach your X server:
#   xhost +local:docker
# and revoke it afterwards:
#   xhost -local:docker
DISPLAY=:0

# --- Plant selection -------------------------------------------------------
# F1 implements diffdrive ONLY. sim.launch.py rejects any other value with an
# explicit error rather than silently starting the wrong robot. `quadruped`
# arrives in F3 and becomes selectable in F6.
ROBOT_TYPE=diffdrive
